@TheCharlatan sometimes mentions [sourcetrail](https://github.com/CoatiSoftware/Sourcetrail) as a tool to visually inspect the currently required kernel headers. I've set it up and figured it could be worth sharing with anyone who's interested in having a quick look to the trail of headers without having to set up the tool themselves.

The list of headers included in libbitcoinkernel as of current master d2ccca253f4294b8f480e1d192913f4985a1af08:
![bitcoin-chainstate_sourcetrail](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/assets/22457751/5dd5c049-35df-4e74-a52f-7453efa5f0e3)

@fanquake Thank you very much! This helped a lot!

What I need is `btck_script_pubkey_verify` function. Unfortunately I can't use the one provided by `src/kernel/bitcoinkernel.cpp` directly, because it is a part of `bitcoinkernel` library which is too large for my use case. It is too large for the guest path: chainstate, LevelDB, filesystem pieces, etc.

That is why I [copy-pasted](https://gist.github.com/starius/16f152b8fd639fb609508ccec4b0e2d0) `btck_script_pubkey_verify` and adapted it for my use case. The only dependencies from Bitcoin Core are now `bitcoin_consensus`, `bitcoin_crypto`, and `secp256k1`.

This works and works great, but I think we can refactor it so stock `btck_script_pubkey_verify` can be used from RISC0 directly:
 - expose a script-only embeddable target containing the official `btck_script_pubkey_verify` without pulling the full kernel source graph
 - make the function **allocation-free** to avoid overrides of `malloc` and friends (see my snippet above)

Inspired by [hyperscan API](https://intel.github.io/hyperscan/dev-reference/api_files.html), I propose the following API:
```c
int btck_script_verify_workspace_size(params..., size_t* out_size);

int btck_script_verify_with_workspace(
      params...,
      char* workspace_ptr,
      size_t workspace_len,
      btck_ScriptVerifyStatus* status
)

// Usage:

size_t workspace_len;
if (!btck_script_verify_workspace_size(..., &workspace_len)) {
  return error;
}

char* workspace_ptr = malloc(workspace_len);
if (workspace_ptr == NULL) {
  return error;
}

btck_ScriptVerifyStatus status;
if (!btck_script_verify_with_workspace(..., workspace_ptr, workspace_len, &status)) {
  return error;
}

// Handle status.
```
